(773865, 83072, 16965, '<td valign="top">I can''t find the focal point of this image, and as such, I cannot determine what the choice is supposed to be.</td>', 'I can''t find the focal point of this image, and as such, I cannot determine what the choice is supposed to be.', '2004-06-22 18:34:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(773866, 84008, 16004, '<td valign="top">well, to be honest i see only three colours, and on a purely personal taste, i don''t find any of the cars particularly exciting...  sorry.    technically though, even considering the lot is well lit, for a night time shot it''s nicely sharp, and the deep depth of field works well.  i would suggest a couple of things, the first concerns the pre-owned flags.  because we see them from the back, eyes are drawn immediately to them in a sub-conscious attempt to decipher the wording, which detracts from the main subjects.  however, by simply flipping the image along the horizontal to get a mirrored-copy, the "pre-owned" flags read correctly and are less an alternative point of interest.  also, when taking the shot i might be inclined to move closer to the cars, and take a shot along their noses.   this would allow you to crop closer to the cars, thereby reducing the amount of concrete filling about a fifth of the shot.  5.</td>', 'well, to be honest i see only three colours, and on a purely personal taste, i don''t find any of the cars particularly exciting...  sorry.    technically though, even considering the lot is well lit, for a night time shot it''s nicely sharp, and the deep depth of field works well.  i would suggest a couple of things, the first concerns the pre-owned flags.  because we see them from the back, eyes are drawn immediately to them in a sub-conscious attempt to decipher the wording, which detracts from the main subjects.  however, by simply flipping the image along the horizontal to get a mirrored-copy, the "pre-owned" flags read correctly and are less an alternative point of interest.  also, when taking the shot i might be inclined to move closer to the cars, and take a shot along their noses.   this would allow you to crop closer to the cars, thereby reducing the amount of concrete filling about a fifth of the shot.  5.', '2004-06-22 18:35:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(773867, 83524, 16965, '<td valign="top">a great idea here, and I like the composition, but the too-shallow DOF killed it, sorry.</td>', 'a great idea here, and I like the composition, but the too-shallow DOF killed it, sorry.', '2004-06-22 18:35:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(773872, 83649, 19751, '<td valign="top">i love this. great job - 9</td>', 'i love this. great job - 9', '2004-06-22 18:39:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(773873, 82981, 16004, '<td valign="top">well, the magazine obvoiusly (you said my choice).  well, not that magazine, but a magazine.  perhaps there''s a magazine about bibles?  would that be a test of faith?  ANYway - why did you cover up the title of the magazine?  i can see it''s health today from the web address at the base!  also, for such a composed shot, a plain boring background would work better, as would slightly less harsh (but perhaps brighter) lighting.  possibly from a window?  shot also seems a tad noisy / grainy / pixelly.  a gentle going over of neatimage works miracles!</td>', 'well, the magazine obvoiusly (you said my choice).  well, not that magazine, but a magazine.  perhaps there''s a magazine about bibles?  would that be a test of faith?  ANYway - why did you cover up the title of the magazine?  i can see it''s health today from the web address at the base!  also, for such a composed shot, a plain boring background would work better, as would slightly less harsh (but perhaps brighter) lighting.  possibly from a window?  shot also seems a tad noisy / grainy / pixelly.  a gentle going over of neatimage works miracles!', '2004-06-22 18:41:29.000000', NULL, 1),
