(775284, 83945, 10390, '<td valign="top">I''m pretty happy with this result for this family-album-snapshot. I know it has many faults and the comments are just right! I wasn''t going to submit in this challenge in the first place, but some hours before deadline I was playing with my son and was teasing him with his pacifiers (he always has two pacifiers in his bed).  I decided to grab my camera without caring much about the light, angle, DOF, etc. I just found his face expression so typical for "choise expression" in this photo.  I decided to submit this photo to finally try out how the challenges work here on this site.  I thought it would maybe be a midrange photo, but I''m very happy for 61 out of 227 and 73%!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-07-05 13:55:46.</i></td>', 'I''m pretty happy with this result for this family-album-snapshot. I know it has many faults and the comments are just right! I wasn''t going to submit in this challenge in the first place, but some hours before deadline I was playing with my son and was teasing him with his pacifiers (he always has two pacifiers in his bed).  I decided to grab my camera without caring much about the light, angle, DOF, etc. I just found his face expression so typical for "choise expression" in this photo.  I decided to submit this photo to finally try out how the challenges work here on this site.  I thought it would maybe be a midrange photo, but I''m very happy for 61 out of 227 and 73%!', '2004-06-23 06:40:59.000000', '2004-07-05 14:55:46.000000', 0),
(775338, 83074, 22677, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the comments, I actually wanted to reshoot this, and try and get the dice moer in focus, perhaps using a flash to freeze the action, but didn''t have time.<br/> <br/>It took me long enough just to get this image :)<br/> <br/>And six 1''s! Blimey!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-23 05:58:27.</i></td>', 'Thank you for all the comments, I actually wanted to reshoot this, and try and get the dice moer in focus, perhaps using a flash to freeze the action, but didn''t have time. It took me long enough just to get this image :) And six 1''s! Blimey!', '2004-06-23 06:57:59.000000', '2004-06-23 06:58:27.000000', 0),
